## ASSEMBLED SECTION



### <img src="https://flagcdn.com/sa.svg" width="32" alt="Saudi Arabia" style={{display: 'inline', verticalAlign: 'middle', position: 'relative', top: '-2px', marginRight: '8px', border: '1px solid #d1d5db', borderRadius: '2px'}} />Saudi Arabia

Saudi Arabia operates as a hyper-centralized petrostate under Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman, who maintains unprecedented personal authority while executing accelerated realistic recalibration of Vision 2030 ambitions. The kingdom demonstrates continued sophisticated triangulation strategy with sustained Western diplomatic engagement (Prince William visit) while Saudi-UAE strategic divergence has materialized in concrete business sector withdrawal from defense cooperation, confirming fundamental Gulf alliance architecture realignment beyond diplomatic disagreement. PIF's revised 2026-2030 strategy emphasizing practical sectors over megaprojects, combined with concrete progress on the $100 billion Jafurah gas project and cabinet adjustments targeting investment performance gaps, demonstrates systematic Vision 2030 recalibration toward selective execution success within realistic fiscal parameters. Critical vulnerabilities persist in geographic concentration of oil infrastructure, dependence on desalinated water, and social contract renegotiation dependent on continuous job creation.

**Key developments:**

- **Diplomatic:** Britain's Prince William met Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman during official visit focused on trade and economic cooperation, requested by British government to strengthen ties with key Middle Eastern ally despite ongoing human rights concerns
- **Diplomatic:** Thirty Emirati entities officially listed as exhibitors but Emirati presence almost nowhere found on show floor, with experts linking absence to deteriorating Saudi-UAE relations over regional issues including Yemen conflict
- **Diplomatic:** Memorandum of understanding signed between Saudi Defense Minister Prince Khalid bin Salman and Somali counterpart, aimed at strengthening defense cooperation as Somalia seeks regional backing against Israel's Somaliland recognition
- **Economic:** Saudi Arabia's $925 billion PIF announced new strategy focusing on logistics, mining, manufacturing, and clean energy while scaling back from some megaprojects, with PIF Forum yielding $16 billion in memorandums of understanding
- **Economic:** Aramco commenced light oil condensate production from massive Jafurah unconventional gas project after completing Phase 1 construction, marking start of kingdom's first major fracking operation with initial cargoes sold to Asian buyers

<Accordion title="Other Stories">
- **DP World CEO Sultan Ahmed bin Sulayem resigns after being named in Epstein files** — Dubai-based port operator DP World announced new leadership after CEO Sultan Ahmed bin Sulayem was identified in recently released Jeffrey Epstein files, showing extensive correspondence between the two men over more than a decade. *([edition.cnn.com](https://edition.cnn.com/2026/02/13/business/epstein-files-bin-sulayem-friendship-intl))*
- **Public Investment Fund unveils revised five-year strategy with focus shift** — Saudi Arabia's $925 billion Public Investment Fund announced a new 2026-2030 strategy focusing more on logistics, mining, manufacturing, and clean energy while scaling back from some megaprojects. The PIF Forum yielded $16 billion in memorandums of understanding. *([reuters.com](https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/saudi-pif-unveil-new-20262030-strategy-this-week-sources-say-2026-02-09/))*
- **World Defense Show 2026 concludes with $8.8 billion in contracts signed** — Saudi Arabia's third World Defense Show in Riyadh ended with over 60 military and defense contracts worth $8.8 billion signed with local and international companies. The event highlighted the kingdom's push to localize 50% of defense spending by 2030. *([saudigazette.com.sa](https://arabnews.com/node/2632798/saudi-arabia))*
- **Saudi Arabia scales back giga-projects including NEOM to focus on 2034 World Cup** — Saudi Arabia is reportedly scaling back ambitious megaprojects including NEOM's 'The Line' to prioritize 2034 World Cup preparations and address budget constraints. Construction contracts dropped nearly 40% as the kingdom reassesses its Vision 2030 priorities. *([agbi.com](https://www.agbi.com/giga-projects/2026/02/saudi-arabia-scales-back-giga-projects-to-focus-on-2034-world-cup/))*
- **Saudi Aramco achieves 70% local content target through iktva program** — Saudi Aramco announced its supply chain transformation program iktva has reached its 70% local content target, contributing $280 billion to GDP and creating over 200,000 jobs. The company plans to increase localization further by 2030. *([english.aawsat.com](https://english.aawsat.com/business/5239816-saudi-aramco-achieves-70-local-content-target-through-iktva-program))*
- **Saudi Arabia and Microsoft sign MoU to advance AI in industrial sector** — Saudi Aramco and Microsoft signed a memorandum of understanding to explore digital initiatives aimed at accelerating artificial intelligence adoption in industrial sectors and enhancing Saudi Arabia's digital sovereignty capabilities. *([techafricanews.com](https://techafricanews.com/2026/02/13/microsoft-and-aramco-deepen-partnership-to-advance-digital-sovereignty-and-ai))*
- **Saudi Foreign Minister holds diplomatic meetings at Munich Security Conference** — Saudi Foreign Minister Prince Faisal bin Farhan attended the Munich Security Conference, meeting with US officials including antisemitism envoy Rabbi Yehuda Kaploun and Syrian counterpart Asaad Al-Shaibani to discuss regional developments and bilateral relations. *([english.aawsat.com](https://english.aawsat.com/gulf/5240958-saudi-fm-meets-us-senior-advisor-syrian-counterpart-munich-security-conference))*
- **Saudi Arabia condemns foreign interference in Sudan amid RSF attacks** — Saudi Arabia reaffirmed support for Sudan's unity and condemned attacks by the Rapid Support Forces in Kordofan states, denouncing foreign interference in the conflict while Saudi air defenses intercepted Iranian drones over the Eastern Province. *([aljazeera.com](https://aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/8/saudi-arabia-slams-foreign-interference-in-sudan-after-deadly-rsf-attacks))*
- **Controlled comeback of Abdullah clan into MBS inner circle** — Prince Mutaib bin Abdullah, former head of the Saudi National Guard and son of late King Abdullah, is making a discreet return to influence within Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman's inner circle after being targeted in the 2017 corruption crackdown. *([intelligenceonline.com](https://intelligenceonline.com/middle-east-and-africa/2026/02/12/the-controlled-comeback-of-the-abdullah-clan-into-mbs-s-inner-circle,110626405-art))*
- **Aston Martin Aramco F1 team unveils 2026 season livery with Honda partnership** — Aston Martin Aramco Formula One Team launched its 2026 season at Ithra in Saudi Arabia, unveiling the AMR26 car livery powered by Honda's RA626H power unit and featuring Aramco's sustainable fuel technology. *([astonmartinf1.com](https://astonmartinf1.com/en-GB/news/announcement/aston-martin-aramco-launches-season-with-livery-reveal))*
